    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0885" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg789"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thiébaut to Mr.
                            Adee.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of France in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                                1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Adee</hi>: Referring to our conversation of
                    day before yesterday, I have the honor to transmit to you herewith for your
                    information copy of a telegram which the ambassador has received from the agent
                    of the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Buena Ventura</hi>, recently captured by
                    the Federal squadron in the Gulf of Mexico: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Liverpool</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 24, 1898</hi>.</p>
                        <p>Not being able to communicate with our <hi rendition="#italic">Buena
                                Ventura</hi>, notwithstanding all efforts made, we beg you to be
                            pleased to indicate to us in what way we can do so. Families
                            anxious.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Larranaga.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>The ambassador would be especially obliged to you if you could enable him to
                    answer this telegram. News of the crew of this vessel might doubtless be
                    obtained either from the Department of the Navy or the Treasury.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thiébaut.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
